<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/</link><lastBuildDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 18:47:27 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>The World This Week</category><title>Can we slowdown AI, and 9/11, who has the right to remember?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-world-this-week/20260911-can-we-slowdown-ai-and-9-11-who-has-the-right-to-remember</link><description>
In a week that marks 25 years since 9/11, Americans paused to pay tribute. Six bells tolled to signify six fatal moments in New York, at the Pentagon and in Pennsylvania, with a seventh bell rung this year to commemorate those who later died from 9/11-related illnesses.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ebcc439a-ae0e-11f1-86c2-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/WhatsApp-Image-2026-09-11-at-20-12-19.jpeg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ebcc439a-ae0e-11f1-86c2-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/WhatsApp-Image-2026-09-11-at-20-12-19.jpeg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">7f09f986-ae05-11f1-8831-3d527545dca5</guid><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 18:43:53 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Gavin LEE</dc:creator></item><item><category>Spotlight</category><title>Spotlight</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20260911-spotlight</link><description>
The New York Times reporter Carol Rosenberg is widely regarded as one of the foremost American journalists, if not the foremost, on the U.S. detention camp at Guantanamo Bay in Cuba, where several alleged suspects in the 9/11 attacks are still being held, including the alleged “architect” of the attacks, alongside three other suspected plotters.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b7aa6a36-ae0b-11f1-af27-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C82H8H8.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b7aa6a36-ae0b-11f1-af27-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C82H8H8.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e77bcd60-ae04-11f1-9883-49544767a90a</guid><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 18:42:54 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Gavin LEE</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Flavio Bolsonaro probed for corruption as Brazil election tightens</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260911-flavio-bolsonaro-probed-for-corruption-as-brazil-election-tightens</link><description>
Just weeks before the vote, Brazilian presidential hopeful Flavio Bolsonaro's campaign is being rocked by revelations he is under investigation for alleged corruption and money laundering. The probe centres on financing sought for a film about his father, former president Jair Bolsonaro, court documents unsealed on Friday showed.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/60346ac2-adf7-11f1-98bc-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-09T171741Z-1887204671-RC2RFNA2JH7L-RTRMADP-3-BRAZIL-ELECTION-BOLSONARO.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/60346ac2-adf7-11f1-98bc-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-09T171741Z-1887204671-RC2RFNA2JH7L-RTRMADP-3-BRAZIL-ELECTION-BOLSONARO.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b070e5a8-adfa-11f1-9d66-817a00b83769</guid><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 16:21:38 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/60346ac2-adf7-11f1-98bc-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-09T171741Z-1887204671-RC2RFNA2JH7L-RTRMADP-3-BRAZIL-ELECTION-BOLSONARO.jpg">© Pilar Olivares, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Trump delivers remarks at Pentagon ceremony to mark 25th anniversary of 9/11</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20260911-trump-delivers-remarks-at-pentagon-ceremony-to-mark-25th-anniversary-of-9-11</link><description>
US President Donald Trump observed Friday’s 25th anniversary by speaking about 9/11 at a ceremony at the Pentagon commemorating the lives lost when al-Qaeda militants hijacked planes and killed nearly 3,000 people in three locations, upending American foreign policy and national security.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3239c8d6-adf4-11f1-b7bf-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/trumpmini.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3239c8d6-adf4-11f1-b7bf-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/trumpmini.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4cc3104a-adf4-11f1-b948-8b0afeaba68e</guid><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 15:29:15 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>25 years after 9/11, al Qaeda remains a threat – even as Washington looks away</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260911-25-years-after-9-11-al-qaeda-remains-threat-washington-looks-away-counter-terrorism</link><description>
A quarter of a century after the deadliest terrorist attacks in US history, al Qaeda’s various branches have moved away from the global jihad advocated by Osama bin Laden, focusing instead on regional insurgencies. Their actions continue to destabilise swathes of the world, from the Sahel to Afghanistan, neglected by a US administration that critics say has unlearned the lessons of 9/11.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fcc9c0b8-ad29-11f1-9521-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP18340343104699.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fcc9c0b8-ad29-11f1-9521-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP18340343104699.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">99e5bb08-ade4-11f1-a201-abb2482cd37a</guid><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 14:24:25 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/fcc9c0b8-ad29-11f1-9521-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP18340343104699.jpg">© Farah Abdi Warsameh, AP file photo</source><dc:creator>Antoine FLANDRIN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Scoop</category><title>How the media has changed since 9/11</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/scoop/20260911-how-the-media-has-changed-since-9-11</link><description>
It has been 25 years since terrorists hijacked planes and flew them into the Twin Towers, the Pentagon, and a fourth crashed in a field in Pennsylvania. Nearly 3,000 people were killed in the attacks that changed the course of US and world history. This week FRANCE 24's media show Scoop looks at how journalists covered 9/11 and how the attacks changed the news industry.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/61d790fa-ade5-11f1-b615-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5942620636aa4032c26b368-44973480.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/61d790fa-ade5-11f1-b615-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-5942620636aa4032c26b368-44973480.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b93df6b4-ade4-11f1-929d-abb2482cd37a</guid><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 13:37:44 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>William HILDERBRANDT</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Vance calls Democrats 'party of hatred' as he seizes MAGA spotlight</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260911-vance-tries-label-democrats-as-party-of-hatred-seizes-maga-spotlight</link><description>
US Vice President JD Vance launched a virulent attack on the Democratic Party Thursday, accusing them of being the "party of hatred" at day two of the Republican convention ahead of the November midterm elections. With public support for President Donald Trump at record lows, Republican figures are increasingly trying to frame their opponents as dangerous political extremists.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4b830b4a-ada4-11f1-ad78-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26254075475865.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4b830b4a-ada4-11f1-ad78-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26254075475865.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">01f37ddc-ada6-11f1-a8c9-0d85900713cb</guid><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 06:45:36 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/4b830b4a-ada4-11f1-ad78-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26254075475865.jpg">© Julia Demaree Nikhinson, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>'That's why we fight': The US marks 25 years since 9/11 attacks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260911-trump-new-york-25-years-9-11-muslim-mayor</link><description>
New York on Friday marked the 25th anniversary of the September 11, 2001 attacks, with US President Donald Trump attending a ceremony at the Pentagon while Vice President JD Vance and four former presidents joined commemorations at Ground Zero, where victims’ relatives will read the names of those killed.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6b04ed90-ade4-11f1-971b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26254445189867.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6b04ed90-ade4-11f1-971b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26254445189867.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f612de0c-ad7f-11f1-a9cf-5ddc1bb97edb</guid><pubDate>Fri, 11 Sep 2026 01:47:42 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/6b04ed90-ade4-11f1-971b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26254445189867.jpg">© Dave Sanders, The New York Times via AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>Meta tests out putting fact-checking in users’ hands across Latin America</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/meta-tests-out-putting-fact-checking-in-users-hands-across-latin-america-1</link><description>
Meta is expanding its shift away from professional fact-checking. The tech giant announced it's trialling it's crowdsourced "Community Notes" system across 16 countries in Latin America. Meta says the system will only fully roll out once it is confident it works, but critics warn that with misinformation, manipulated images and AI-generated content spreading rapidly, crowdsourced checks may come too late to prevent false claims from reaching millions. Vedika Bahl explains the risks.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bc86acb0-ad50-11f1-baa9-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-12835300406aa309c93f4154-74074622.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bc86acb0-ad50-11f1-baa9-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-12835300406aa309c93f4154-74074622.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1d5c19aa-ad4f-11f1-8947-39b0630bb3ec</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 20:11:31 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Vedika BAHL</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>As New York marks 25 years since 9/11, Muslims recall stigmatisation in aftermath of attacks</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/as-new-york-marks-25-years-since-9-11-muslims-recall-stigmatization-in-aftermath-of-attacks</link><description>
As New York marks 25 years since the terrorist attacks on September 11th, New York’s Muslim community has become increasingly part of the fabric of the city. One sign of that is the election of Zohran Mamdani as the city’s mayor last November. Another is the state's largest mosque, due to open its doors at the end of the year. But while things have improved, many Muslims still remember the difficult months that followed the attack. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/05bcffd2-11c1-11ec-9063-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000_9MG36Z.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/05bcffd2-11c1-11ec-9063-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000_9MG36Z.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ace33aca-ad4c-11f1-9f80-39b0630bb3ec</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 19:32:33 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>The Debate</category><title>9/11 then and now: Do September 2001 attacks still shape our world?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/the-debate/20260910-9-11-then-and-now-do-september-2001-attacks-still-shape-our-world</link><description>
Once in a generation – sometimes once in a lifetime – a singular event blindsides the entire planet. 25 years on, does the memory of the 9/11 attacks on New York's Twin Towers, the Pentagon and in Pennsylvania fade into history, or is it still as raw and vivid as on that sunny September morning? 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a2e30182-ad41-11f1-8a5c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-10T000955Z-1465141223-RC2YFNAS0O3V-RTRMADP-3-USA-SEPT11-MEMORIAL.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a2e30182-ad41-11f1-8a5c-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-10T000955Z-1465141223-RC2YFNAS0O3V-RTRMADP-3-USA-SEPT11-MEMORIAL.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fd16ebdc-ad41-11f1-9846-39e6bfb413de</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 18:17:34 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>François PICARD</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>What to know about Trump's pledge of $5,000 to 'every American' if GOP wins midterms</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260910-what-to-know-about-trump-s-5-000-dividend-pledge</link><description>
President Donald Trump ⁠promised a $5,000 "Trump dividend" ​payment to every US adult on Wednesday if his Republicans retain control of the House of Representatives and the Senate in the November 3 midterm elections. The pledge has raised numerous questions. Here's what we know so far. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/88cf8642-ad3e-11f1-a644-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/b62211bb909886fc2d314fba0eb844aa0f37ca66.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/88cf8642-ad3e-11f1-a644-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/b62211bb909886fc2d314fba0eb844aa0f37ca66.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8aa4d2e2-ad3e-11f1-a538-8fbd31854a2a</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 17:39:13 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/88cf8642-ad3e-11f1-a644-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/b62211bb909886fc2d314fba0eb844aa0f37ca66.jpg">© Ronaldo Schemidt, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Focus</category><title>Montserrat: The 'Pompeii' of the Caribbean</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20260910-montserrat-the-pompeii-of-the-caribbean</link><description>
Part of the island of Montserrat, a UK Overseas Territory, was buried by a volcanic eruption in 1995. Today, caution is essential for those venturing on the mysterious island that is full of spectacular Caribbean landscapes. Our colleagues at France Télévisions and FRANCE 24's Florent Marchais report.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d114d97c-ac4c-11f1-a0d7-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/montserrat-volcano-frz-focus.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/d114d97c-ac4c-11f1-a0d7-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/montserrat-volcano-frz-focus.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">55320db0-ac52-11f1-99f2-515e3382455e</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 13:58:36 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE 2</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Colombia court orders President de la Espriella to hide social media videos of him with dead bodies</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260910-colombia-court-orders-president-de-la-espriella-to-hide-social-media-videos-of-him-with-dead-bodies</link><description>
Colombia's right-wing President Abelardo de la Espriella has been ordered to hide social media videos showing him walking past rows of the dead bodies of alleged guerrillas killed by the country's armed forces, according to a court document seen Wednesday. The newly sworn-in president has launched a fresh offensive at armed groups involved in the country's lucrative cocaine trade. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/51dbf7c8-acf4-11f1-92e9-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26238627978322.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/51dbf7c8-acf4-11f1-92e9-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26238627978322.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">744a1a40-acfb-11f1-8727-bfbc394ea958</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 11:31:34 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/51dbf7c8-acf4-11f1-92e9-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26238627978322.jpg">© Fernando Vergara, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Press Review</category><title>'Egomaniac': Papers discuss 'Trumpapalooza' midterm convention</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/egomaniac-papers-discuss-trumpapalooza-midterm-convention</link><description>
PRESS REVIEW – Thursday, September 10: US papers react to the first night of the Republicans' midterm convention in Dallas. Also: five baby orangutans from Southeast Asia have been found in a forest in India. Then some dystopian science news. Finally, perhaps we don't need to do as much sport as we think we do.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/028cf77a-acdc-11f1-a1e2-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Anglais-2026-09-10T05-20-03-244Z.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/028cf77a-acdc-11f1-a1e2-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/Anglais-2026-09-10T05-20-03-244Z.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">158d6656-ace2-11f1-8d6c-5ddb31a6d22f</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 08:39:00 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Elitsa GADEVA</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Trump can see the writing on the wall here': Republicans hold midterm convention</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/trump-can-see-the-writing-on-the-wall-here-republicans-hold-midterm-convention</link><description>
FRANCE 24's Washington, DC correspondent Fraser Jackson weighs in on US President Donald Trump's efforts to leverage his fading star power to help the Republican Party hold onto Congress in November's midterm elections.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/803bf8cc-acd9-11f1-9af0-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260910-060221-060735-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/803bf8cc-acd9-11f1-9af0-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260910-060221-060735-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">859694ee-acd9-11f1-86d4-a57436531fba</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 05:39:41 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>How a former BAPS temple worker in the US got his freedom, but still seeks justice</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260910-how-a-former-baps-temple-worker-in-the-us-got-his-freedom-but-still-seeks-justice</link><description>
The Bochasanwasi Akshar Purushottam Swaminarayan Sanstha (BAPS) Hindu sect at the heart of the Eiffel Tower strike made headlines in France during the inauguration of its latest temple near Paris. In the US, BAPS came under the spotlight when Indian stone workers were rescued from a temple construction site. One former worker recounts his journey and fight for justice.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b94fddcc-ac6b-11f1-bfce-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP23325500348361.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b94fddcc-ac6b-11f1-bfce-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP23325500348361.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f788bf0a-ac6b-11f1-a778-8d898541b3b4</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 05:37:12 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b94fddcc-ac6b-11f1-bfce-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP23325500348361.jpg">© Ted Shaffrey, AP</source><dc:creator>Leela JACINTO</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Trump says he'll give Americans $5,000 each if Republicans win midterm elections</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260910-trump-says-give-americans-5-000-each-if-republicans-win-midterm-elections</link><description>
US President Donald Trump on Wednesday urged his supporters to pretend he was on the ballot in the upcoming midterm elections in November, even saying he would give $5,000 to each American adult if the right-wing Republicans maintain control of Congress. Trump is struggling with low opinion ratings as the cost of living soars and his months-long war against Iran drags on.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a5dd998a-acc7-11f1-b6c0-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26253063907545.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a5dd998a-acc7-11f1-b6c0-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26253063907545.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">60271dec-acd3-11f1-96e1-2fb102e5c7c9</guid><pubDate>Thu, 10 Sep 2026 05:15:57 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/a5dd998a-acc7-11f1-b6c0-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26253063907545.jpg">© Tony Gutierrez, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Brazil Supreme Court chief suspends colleagues' rulings amid election row</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260909-brazil-supreme-court-chief-suspends-rival-rulings-amid-election-row</link><description>
The chief justice of Brazil's Supreme Court stepped in Wednesday to halt conflicting rulings by two fellow judges as a dispute over alleged links between Justice Alexandre de Moraes and a banker accused of fraud deepened. The clash has spilled into the campaign for next month's presidential election, adding to tensions around the court.
